From: Haru <noreply@haru.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] worker : add the battle request, two conversations of one model that hear each other

The battle request holds two conversations of the loaded dialogue model and
steps them in lockstep: in frame t each hears the other's frame t - 1, at the
model's rate, without audio from the caller. Each frame of each speaker goes
out as a chunk with "speaker" (0 or 1, the index in "speakers") beside seq, pcm
and text, and end carries the frames. max_frames sets each conversation's
max_seconds, so that the keys and values held are those of the battle alone.
A hang_up, a cancel or the end of stdin stops it after whole frames; ready
lists "features":["battle"] for a dialogue model. Protocol 4 is unchanged for
every other request. Adds worker-battle-check (the reading and the lockstep on
fake speakers, no model), worker-inbox-check (the inbox on battle lines, no
model) and checks/smoke/worker_battle_smoke.py.

---
